From 8b561eab8ce35fa6b8a319388882dc47e0171cf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:38:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace Google Sheets CMS with Decap CMS admin panel

Adds a real login-protected admin UI at /admin (Decap CMS + Netlify
Identity + Git Gateway) so content can be edited through forms with
image upload instead of a spreadsheet.

- Extract the 4 embedded base64 images out of image-data.js into real
  files under images/, so they can be swapped via upload
- Migrate all content-data.js content into content/*.json (one file
  per section: conditions, treatments, doctor bio, education, videos,
  testimonials, reviews, site text, site images)
- Add content-loader.js to replace sheets-loader.js, fetching the new
  local JSON instead of the published Google Sheet CSV, using the
  same merge/render pipeline as before
- Add admin/index.html + admin/config.yml defining 9 Decap CMS
  collections mapped field-for-field to the new JSON files
- Wire up Netlify Identity login/redirect on both index.html and the
  admin page
- Update the service worker precache list for the new files and
  bump the cache version

content-data.js and data.js are left in place as the baked-in
fallback, matching the site's existing resilience pattern.
